# Credentials for the exercises in harness/. Copy this file to .env beside the package.
#
# Both come from the Synergy Wholesale control panel, under API access.
SW_RESELLER_ID=
SW_API_KEY=

# There is no SW_DELIVER, and that is deliberate.
#
# Every other harness in ~/packages has a switch here that turns the real side effect on,
# because the exercises there can send or write and default to a sink. This one cannot:
# harness/lib/ReadOnlyTransport.php holds an allowlist of eleven operations verified
# read-only against the v3.16 API documentation, and every call goes through it. An
# operation not on that list does not reach the network, and no environment variable
# turns it on, because there is none to set.
#
# That is the right trade for this API. Its write operations register domains, transfer
# them between registrars, pay redemption fees and email real registrants - a flag
# protects the exercise that has it, and does nothing about the exercise that calls the
# wrong method by mistake.
#
# If a write exercise is ever added it needs a switch of its own, refused under an agent
# by harness_agent_refuses() in harness/lib/agent.php. Name it after what it unlocks,
# document it here as NOT belonging in .env, and read the note in that file first.

# Note on the IP whitelist. Synergy Wholesale authorises by IP address as well as by key,
# so a correct key from an unlisted address fails with ERR_RESELLER_NOT_AUTHORISED, which
# reads like a bad key. This box is not a production server. Unless its address has been
# added deliberately, that error is expected here and means nothing is broken.
